WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.188
The XRP Ledger's rules do change, but never quietly.

2
00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:08.615
New features arrive as amendments, and this is how they switch on.

3
00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:14.952
A new feature is written into the server software, and then validators vote on it.

4
00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:20.043
It switches on only after it keeps at least eighty percent support for two weeks in a row.

5
00:00:21.743 --> 00:00:27.015
A server that has not upgraded when an amendment switches on becomes amendment blocked.

6
00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:30.105
It stops following the ledger until it is upgraded.

7
00:00:31.805 --> 00:00:40.206
Many features in this course arrived this way: pools, clawback, N F Ts, credentials, permissioned domains and deep freeze.

8
00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:44.200
Each X L S number is the public proposal behind a feature.

9
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.597
And what is enabled today can always be read from the ledger itself.
